Pros
1. You can pledge money for trading with very good margin. 
2. Adding more and more features. Recently added SWP.

Cons
1. You can not control anything from AMC due to units in demat form.
2. You can not pledge units to third party institutions like Mirae, Bajaj etc. for borrowing money.
3. NAV update is very slow. Other platforms are much faster in NAV updates but may be this is not important for every investors but as a reliable platform, NAV must be updated on time. 

I would suggest here first understand the requirements and then select the most suitable platform for mutual fund investment.', 'unknown', 'en', NULL, 'f916a673bf57300bbd25f5de79349245a98ff27c420c697a39b2d0c164d6c9ac', 'NORMALIZED', 'CLEAN', 'IN', '2.6.2', 3, '2024-08-13 02:33:25', NULL, '2026-11-06 16:11:35', NULL, NULL, 'ELIGIBLE', '1.0.0', '2027-11-06 16:11:35', 'ACTIVE', '2026-11-06 16:11:35', 'This first thing everyone should understand about coin is mutual fund units are stored in demat form and you must need demat account first. You can efficiently use this platform if you are a trader otherwise if you want to just invest in mutual funds then this may not be suitable for you. 

