In the name of "upgrading," they have made basic navigation unnecessarily complicated. Finding standard services and essential portfolio details takes way too much effort now. The home page is crowded with irrelevant features that many of us never asked for:
 Unsolicited F&O & Strategy Tools: Pushing complex options trading strategies and trade ideas directly onto the homepage clutter is useless for long-term investors. Anyone who actively trades F&O already knows what tools they need; forcing it on everyone else just creates noise.
 Intrusive "Expert Advice" & Mutual Fund SIPs: Putting aggressive recommendations front and center makes the app feel cheap and chaotic. If someone wants to start a Mutual Fund SIP, they will intentionally navigate to the MF section—it doesn''t need to take over the main screen.
Upstox needs to realize that adding more clutter isn''t an upgrade—it''s bad UX. Making the app hard to understand for simple, long-term investors will only drive customers away. If this bloated interface continues to prioritize pushed features over clean usability, I will consider closing my Demat account and shifting my portfolio to a simpler competitor.', 'unknown', 'en', NULL, '47879d0864166b2a6ce85e08641b45dae48ca59f28c9b0857191f95e5008ceb2', 'NORMALIZED', 'CLEAN', 'IN', '3.13.0', 1, '2026-09-11 13:20:03', NULL, '2026-11-06 16:11:57', NULL, NULL, 'ELIGIBLE', '1.0.0', '2027-11-06 16:11:57', 'ACTIVE', '2026-11-06 16:11:57', 'As a long-time Upstox user, I am extremely disappointed with the direction this app is heading. I am not a daily day trader; I simply invest manage my portfolio, invest, and close the app until the next time. Upstox used to be great for this, but the recent design changes have turned a once-clean platform into a cluttered mess.
